.TH AL 1 "September 2026" "al" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
al \- manage AnyList lists and items
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B al
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B al
reads and manages AnyList lists, items, and categories.
Use
.B al --help
and command-specific help for available operations and flags.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --json
Print one JSON result with ok, data, and error fields.
.TP
.B --help
Show command help without authentication or network access.
.TP
.B --version
Show the installed version without authentication or network access.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ANYLIST_EMAIL
AnyList account email for network commands.
.TP
.B ANYLIST_PASSWORD
AnyList account password for network commands.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable terminal styling when nonempty.
.SH FILES
The nonsecret configuration is stored in the operating system's user
configuration directory under al/config.json.
On Linux this is $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/al/config.json, or
$HOME/.config/al/config.json when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset.
Credentials remain in process memory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Configuration, selection, authentication, transport, or operation failure.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command or input.
.SH NOTES
This client uses AnyList's unofficial protocol.
Service changes can break compatibility.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full examples and protocol notices are installed under /usr/share/doc/al.
